Subject: Re: Integration follow-up: SDK/auth/routing + observability hooks

Thanks — appreciate the specifics, Sam. Responses inline and a tiny code snippet you can copy into SRE's tests.

- Latency breakdown: most variability at the moment is compute + batch formation. In our hosted environment we expose per-request X-Redwood-Latency header with three numbers: queue_ms|exec_ms|send_ms. Typical breakouts for rerank-weighted workloads: queue 5–20ms, exec 30–80ms, send 5–20ms depending on token counts. We'll run a short benchmark in us-west-2 pinned to a specific model and share numbers.

- Auth: short-lived API keys via Vault is good — we support an STS token exchange flow. We'll provide a sample exchange endpoint and config for your Vault team.

- SDK snippet (Node) — put this behind your service auth to attach x-rw-trace-id and capture latency header: 

const rw = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new rw.Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, region: 'us-west-2' });

async function rerank(query, candidates, traceId) {
  const resp = await client.models.rerank.create({
    model: 'redwood/reranker-v1-q4',
    input: { query, candidates },
    headers: { 'x-rw-trace-id': traceId }
  });
  // response.headers['X-Redwood-Latency'] -> "5|42|8" 
  // record response.headers['X-Redwood-Latency'] and resp.meta.tokens to your logs
  return resp;
}

- Tool-calling handshake: we'll provide a tiny webhook that validates signed callbacks (HMAC) and returns OK; this is covered in integration-qa.pdf (attached).

Proposed tech sync: Thu 04 Mar 2026 10:30 PT (I can move). I've invited Karthik (infra) and Vivek (solutions) to be on the call so we can run a short demo and run a small benchmark live.

Attaching: integration-qa.pdf (QA checklist + HMAC example) and the Postman collection.

